# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/upload-p0 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the
# cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-upload-p0-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the branch (the next2-1 stack plus qwen_device_zeros, qwen_lazy_shard and
# the six upload twins of the production profile, docs/tp4-fabric-upload.md P0 and P1a); substitute it in every template with one command (sed -i 's/tp4-upload-p0-1/<tag>/' *.env).
# The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent (production is down by the owner's choice while it runs).
# A2 (STOP): the AUDITED ATTACH SMOKE of the lazy shard loader (QWEN_FAST_LAZY_SHARD_W=1 + QWEN_FAST_LAZY_SHARD_W_AUDIT=1, qwen_lazy_shard): a weight-cache hit does no host bf16 transpose; the first two loads are compared
# byte for byte (per chip, packed) with the stock host conversion. RUN AFTER A0, which leaves the weight cache warm. READ: '[PINDIAG] tp4 lazy shard engaged', two '[PINDIAG] tp4 lazy shard audit exact=True', NO
# 'audit mismatch' or 'refused', the last '[PINDIAG] tp4 lazy shard loads' line with misses=0 (every load a hit; a cold cache shows misses and says the arm was not run warm), c2_smoke_check clean, the warmup and coding
# answers equal A0's token for token. Stop rule.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-upload-p0-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic-lazy-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
# Knowingly omits concurrent8_steady: without this key c2_serving_job.py refuses the job. The smoke check is unchanged, so the run still ends red on its eight-seat rule; read the logs.
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=audited attach arm (exactness reads on the warmup and coding answers): its test list is fixed by the pack protocol, so concurrent8_steady is not run
